{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":62300,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-opus-5-5","packSha":"4f6cee134559d78f4144683de91971239779e8f3c660ec39b02851d46148ae29","packTokens":32672,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":255,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"intent","tokens":699,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":786,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"assumptions","tokens":2018,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"cb","tokens":446,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"spec","tokens":28351,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":7,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"critic"},"pointers":[],"system":"Adversarial reviewer. Find defects in this spec; don't praise; don't rewrite it.\nRubric: 1 conflicts between requirements 2 missing error, empty and permission paths 3 ACs not observable at a public surface 4 scope creep beyond the intent 5 claims about existing behaviour without anchors 6 state transitions and existing data 7 behaviour changes outside the requested scope (blast radius) 8 hardcoded identifiers that should be configuration.\nEach finding: rubric number, reqId, severity (critical|high|medium|low), one-sentence evidence in \"finding\". Empty list if none.\nThe human answered questions and accepted assumptions (below). Scope they decided is not a defect: don't flag it.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"intent\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"changeClass\": \"feature\",\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-06T22:47:10.343Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"intent\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"model\": \"claude-haiku-4-5\",\n   \"stage\": \"intake\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20261006-boutique-fitness-studio-class-b497\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"rigor\": \"full\",\n \"risk\": \"high\",\n \"riskTags\": [\n  \"payments\",\n  \"pii\",\n  \"auth\"\n ],\n \"source\": \"cli\",\n \"spans\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-1\",\n   \"text\": \"A responsive web app for Pulse Studio, a single-location boutique fitness studio offering yoga, pilates, HIIT, spin, and boxing classes\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-2\",\n   \"text\": \"Members browse the weekly class schedule, view class details, book or cancel a spot, join a waitlist when a class is full\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-3\",\n   \"text\": \"3 screens: Schedule (home), Class Detail, My Bookings\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-4\",\n   \"text\": \"Enforce the studio's booking and cancellation rules: capacity, waitlist, 7-day booking window, 15-minute pre-start window, 2-hour cancellation window, no overlaps, 10-booking limit\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-5\",\n   \"text\": \"Seed data covering current and next week: at least 40 class sessions, 5 instructors, full classes, cancelled classes, demo member with bookings\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-6\",\n   \"text\": \"Bookings must survive page reload via backend or local persistence\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-7\",\n   \"text\": \"Design quality as primary criterion: boutique aesthetic, warm off-white background, per-class-type accent colours, dark mode support, WCAG AA contrast\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-8\",\n   \"text\": \"Full keyboard navigation, screen reader support, semantic structure, 44×44 px touch targets\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-9\",\n   \"text\": \"Automated tests for business rules and end-to-end test\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-10\",\n   \"text\": \"Mobile-first responsive from 360 px, tablet 2-column, desktop side panel\"\n  }\n ],\n \"touchesUi\": true\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Where does Back go from Class Detail?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Back to the screen Class Detail was opened from (Schedule or My Bookings), keeping that screen's state\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which rules apply when joining a waitlist?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The same 7-day and 15-minute windows plus the past and studio-cancelled rules as booking; overlap and the 10-booking limit are only checked at promotion\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"How does Undo work on the 5-second booking toast?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Undo removes the booking as if it was never made: no cancellation record, no late-cancel warning, counts restored\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How is the 7-day booking window measured?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Booking is allowed if the class starts within 7×24 hours from now (Europe/London)\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"There is only one real member, so how is waitlist promotion modelled and shown?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Other members exist only as booked and waitlist counts. When Alex cancels, the booked count stays the same and the waitlist count drops by one. Alex's own promotion is triggered by a test/demo hook that simulates another member cancelling\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Are the seed dates fixed calendar dates, or worked out from today's date when the app first loads?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Worked out from today (Europe/London) on first load, then stored\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Is a late cancellation ('counts as a missed class') stored differently and shown in Past or the stats?\",\n  \"answer\": \"It is stored as Cancelled with a late flag and shown in Past as 'Late cancel'; stats are unaffected\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Nobody on staff can mark attendance, so what happens to a Booked class once it has finished?\",\n  \"answer\": \"It moves to Past and is shown and counted as Attended automatically\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"assumptions\" kind=\"assumptions\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q2\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-10\",\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-1\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"When must the Class Detail action footer stay visible? → assumed: Pinned to the bottom on mobile at every scroll position; normal placement in the tablet and desktop side panel\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q4\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-4\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-2\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"What happens if the first person on the waitlist can't be promoted, because the promotion would overlap another Booked class, take them past the 10-booking limit, or the class starts within 15 minutes? → assumed: Skip that member: they stay waitlisted and the next eligible person is promoted\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q6\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-4\",\n   \"I-9\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-3\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"How is a late cancellation (inside 2 hours) recorded? → assumed: Status becomes Cancelled and a late-cancellation flag is set; Past shows a 'Late cancel' badge\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q7\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-5\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-4\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"There is no staff UI, so how do Booked bookings become Attended? → assumed: They are marked Attended automatically once the class has ended\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q9\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-6\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-5\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"How are seed dates tied to 'current week and next week'? → assumed: Seed dates are generated relative to the date of first load in Europe/London and then persisted\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q10\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-6\",\n   \"I-4\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-6\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"Which persistence approach should be used? → assumed: Browser local storage behind a business-rules/data module that every action goes through\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q12\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-4\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-7\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Do back-to-back classes overlap (one ends 18:45, the next starts 18:45)? → assumed: No: only a real overlap in time is a conflict\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q13\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-8\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What happens to Alex's booking or waitlist entry on a class the studio has cancelled? → assumed: Never seed Alex onto a studio-cancelled class, so the case can't happen\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q14\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-5\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-9\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"How far can the week arrows on the Schedule move? → assumed: Only the current week and next week (arrows disabled beyond them)\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q15\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-10\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which time-of-day filter does a class starting at exactly 17:00 fall into? → assumed: Afternoon is 12:00–16:59 and Evening is 17:00 onward\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q16\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-11\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Does the 'Upcoming' stat tile count waitlisted classes? → assumed: Only upcoming Booked classes\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"browsers\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q17\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-10\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-12\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which browsers must be supported? → assumed: The latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"hosting\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q18\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-6\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-13\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Where should the app run or be hosted for this release? → assumed: One cloud region, in the client's cloud account.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-4\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-14\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"When the demo hook promotes Alex from the waitlist but the promotion would break the overlap rule or the 10-booking limit, what happens? → assumed: Alex stays waitlisted at #1 and the next member is promoted instead; Alex sees why\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-6\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-15\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which persistence should be used? → assumed: Browser local storage, with no backend\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-16\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Can people see the waitlist promotion demo hook in the app? → assumed: Tests only, with no UI\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-17\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Do joining a waitlist, cancelling and leaving a waitlist also show a toast with Undo, or only booking? → assumed: Only inline booking shows a toast with Undo; the others show a plain confirmation toast\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-4\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-18\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Do two classes that touch end to start (one ends at 18:45, the next starts at 18:45) count as overlapping? → assumed: No. Only real time overlap is rejected\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-4\",\n   \"I-5\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-19\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"If the studio cancels a class that Alex has booked or is waitlisted for, how does My Bookings show it? → assumed: It moves to Past with the status 'Cancelled by studio'\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-5\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-20\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"How far can the day strip go back and forward with the week arrows, and which day does a week start on? → assumed: Monday to Sunday weeks, limited to the current and next week\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"cb\" kind=\"current-behaviour\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"claims\": [],\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-06T22:47:10.389Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"current-behaviour\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"stage\": \"ground\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20261006-boutique-fitness-studio-class-b497\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"notFound\": [\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-1\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-2\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-3\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-4\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-5\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-6\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-7\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-8\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-9\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-10\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"ears\": \"The booking app shall be a responsive web app for the single-location boutique studio Pulse Studio offering Yoga, Pilates, HIIT, Spin and Boxing classes, presenting exactly three screens, Schedule (the home screen at the root URL), Class Detail and My Bookings, for the single pre-signed-in member Alex Rivera with no sign-in screen, under a top bar that shows the \\\"Pulse Studio\\\" wordmark and the member avatar with initials \\\"AR\\\" linking to My Bookings.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-3\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A fresh browser with no stored app data\",\n     \"when\": \"The app root URL is opened\",\n     \"then\": \"The Schedule screen is shown, the top bar displays the text \\\"Pulse Studio\\\" and an avatar with the text \\\"AR\\\", and no sign-in page is shown\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n     \"given\": \"The Schedule screen is shown\",\n     \"when\": \"The \\\"AR\\\" avatar is activated\",\n     \"then\": \"The My Bookings screen is shown with the name \\\"Alex Rivera\\\" and the membership \\\"Unlimited Monthly\\\"\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.3\",\n     \"given\": \"The Schedule screen is shown at a 360 px wide viewport\",\n     \"when\": \"A person looks at the class type filter chips\",\n     \"then\": \"Exactly five type chips are displayed, labelled \\\"Yoga\\\", \\\"Pilates\\\", \\\"HIIT\\\", \\\"Spin\\\" and \\\"Boxing\\\", and no other studio location is shown anywhere on the page\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A clock of 2026-10-06T23:30Z (00:30 on 7 October in Europe/London)\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned date is 2026-10-07\",\n     \"when\": \"The booking service's today value is read\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A session starting at 2026-10-07T17:30Z\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned text is \\\"18:30\\\"\",\n     \"when\": \"The time formatter is called for it\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A class starting at 18:30 London time\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.3\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"The card displays \\\"18:30\\\"\",\n     \"when\": \"A person views its card on a device set to a US timezone and 12-hour clock\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The booking app shall work out \\\"today\\\", day boundaries and every time-based rule in the Europe/London timezone and show all times in 24-hour HH:mm format.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"Q-4\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A fixed clock of Wednesday 2026-10-07 10:00 Europe/London\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned session list has a count of at least 40, includes every one of the 5 class types and 3 rooms, and the returned instructor list has a count of 5, each with a name, a bio and an avatar\",\n     \"when\": \"The seed generator is called\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The same returned seed data\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.2\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The count of sessions with booked count equal to capacity is at least 3, the count with 1–3 free spots is at least 3, and the count with status \\\"Cancelled by studio\\\" is at least 1\",\n     \"when\": \"Sessions are counted by availability\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The same returned seed data\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.3\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"Exactly 2 records are Booked on sessions starting after now, 1 record is Waitlisted with a waitlist position value, 3 records are Attended on sessions that ended before now, and no record refers to a session with status \\\"Cancelled by studio\\\"\",\n     \"when\": \"Alex Rivera's booking records are read\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The same returned seed data\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.4\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"Every session record has a name, type, intensity of Low/Medium/High, instructor, room, start date-time, a duration value of 30, 45, 60 or 75, capacity, booked count, waitlist count, a 2–4 sentence description, a non-empty what-to-bring list and a status\",\n     \"when\": \"Each session's fields are read\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When the seed generator runs, the booking service shall return seed data containing at least 40 class sessions across the types Yoga, Pilates, HIIT, Spin and Boxing and the rooms Studio A, Studio B and Spin Room, 5 instructors with name, bio and avatar, at least 3 full sessions, at least 3 sessions with 1–3 spots left, at least 1 session with status \\\"Cancelled by studio\\\", and for demo member Alex Rivera 2 upcoming Booked bookings, 1 Waitlisted booking and 3 past Attended bookings, none of them on a studio-cancelled session.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"ASM-8\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"ears\": \"When the app loads, the booking service shall generate the seed sessions dated within the current Monday–Sunday week and the next week, both measured from the load date in Europe/London, and store them in browser local storage if no stored data exists, or reuse the stored sessions with their IDs and start times unchanged if stored seed data already exists.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"Q-6\",\n    \"ASM-5\",\n    \"ASM-20\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n     \"given\": \"Empty local storage and a fixed clock of Wednesday 2026-10-07 10:00 Europe/London\",\n     \"when\": \"The booking service is initialised\",\n     \"then\": \"Every returned schedule session start date falls between Monday 2026-10-05 00:00 and Sunday 2026-10-18 23:59 Europe/London (sessions referenced only by Alex's past Attended bookings may be earlier), and local storage holds a stored record of the sessions\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n     \"given\": \"Local storage already holds data seeded on 2026-10-07\",\n     \"when\": \"The booking service is initialised with a clock of 2026-10-09\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned sessions have the same IDs and start times as the stored data\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"One booking service instance has booked one class, cancelled another late and joined a waitlist at position 3 over a given local storage\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned lists contain the same 3 records with the same status, late flag and waitlist position values, and the returned session count values match\",\n     \"when\": \"A new instance is created over the same storage and the bookings are read\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Alex has booked a class through the Schedule screen\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.2\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"The class card button is shown as \\\"Booked ✓\\\" and the class is listed under Upcoming in My Bookings with a \\\"Booked\\\" badge\",\n     \"when\": \"The page is reloaded\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When any booking action changes data, the booking service shall write bookings, statuses, late flags, session counts and waitlist positions to browser local storage before reporting success, so a new instance over the same storage, or a page reload, returns the same data.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"ASM-6\",\n    \"ASM-15\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Session \\\"Sunrise Vinyasa\\\" with capacity 20, booked count 18, starting in 2 days, with no conflicts\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned record has status Booked, a booking ID and a created date-time, and the session's returned booked count value is 19\",\n     \"when\": \"book(session) is called\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The booking from AC-6.1 has been made\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned Upcoming list contains the Sunrise Vinyasa record with status Booked\",\n     \"when\": \"The bookings are read\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When Alex books a Scheduled session that has free spots, starts within the booking window, does not overlap another Booked session of Alex's and keeps Alex at or under 10 upcoming Booked sessions, the booking service shall create one Booked record with an ID and created date-time and increase the session's booked count by 1.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"ASM-6\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A session with capacity 20 and booked count 10\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The second call returns an \\\"already booked\\\" error, the returned booking list has exactly 1 record for the session, and the booked count value is 11\",\n     \"when\": \"book(S) is called twice in a row with no wait between them\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Alex is Waitlisted on a full session\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned error is \\\"already booked\\\" and the waitlist count value is unchanged\",\n     \"when\": \"joinWaitlist is called again for that session\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The Schedule screen shows a bookable class\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.3\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"My Bookings shows exactly one row for that class\",\n     \"when\": \"A person taps its Book button twice within 300 ms\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If Alex already holds a Booked or Waitlisted record for a session, then the booking service shall reject a further book or join-waitlist request for that session with an \\\"already booked\\\" error without creating a record or changing counts.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-4\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Session \\\"Power HIIT\\\" with capacity 16 and booked count 16\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned error is \\\"class full\\\", no Booked record is created, and the booked count value stays 16\",\n     \"when\": \"book(session) is called\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If a session's booked count equals its capacity, then the booking service shall reject a book request with a \\\"class full\\\" error and leave the booked and waitlist counts unchanged.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"ears\": \"When Alex requests to join the waitlist of a Scheduled session that starts within the booking window, the booking service shall either create a Waitlisted record whose position equals the previous waitlist count plus 1 and increase the waitlist count by 1, without checking the overlap rule or the 10-booking limit, when the session is full, or reject the request with a not-full error when the session has free spots.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"Q-2\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n     \"given\": \"Session \\\"Power HIIT\\\" is full with waitlist count 2 and starts tomorrow\",\n     \"when\": \"joinWaitlist(session) is called\",\n     \"then\": \"The returned record has status Waitlisted with position value 3, and the session's waitlist count value is 3\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A full session that overlaps a session Alex has Booked, and Alex holds 10 upcoming Booked sessions\",\n     \"when\": \"joinWaitlist(session) is called\",\n     \"then\": \"